reference:
Inline styles can't contain media queries, so you have two main options: a CSS class, or Ant Design's `Grid.useBreakpoint` hook.

## Option 1: CSS class (simplest)

Note that Ant Design's `sm` breakpoint begins at 576px, and `md` begins at 768px. Since your layout switches to two columns at `md`, "sm or smaller" means `max-width: 767px`.

```jsx
<Col xs={24} sm={24} md={12} className="hero-image-col">
  <img
    src={heroimg}
    alt="كريبتو تاسكي"
    style={{ width: "100%", maxHeight: '400px', objectFit: "cover" }}
  />
</Col>
```

```css
/* styles.css */
@media (max-width: 767px) {
  .hero-image-col {
    margin-top: 30px;
  }
}
```

## Option 2: `Grid.useBreakpoint` hook (no CSS file)

```jsx
import { Grid } from 'antd';

const { useBreakpoint } = Grid;

function Hero() {
  const screens = useBreakpoint();
  const isSmallOrLess = !screens.md; // true when width < 768px

  return (
    <Row justify="space-around" align="middle">
      <Col xs={24} sm={24} md={12}>
        {/* first column content */}
      </Col>

      <Col
        xs={24}
        sm={24}
        md={12}
        style={{ marginTop: isSmallOrLess ? '30px' : 0 }}
      >
        <img
          src={heroimg}
          alt="كريبتو تاسكي"
          style={{ width: "100%", maxHeight: '400px', objectFit: "cover" }}
        />
      </Col>
    </Row>
  );
}
```

`screens.md` is `true` when the viewport is ≥ 768px, so `!screens.md` covers both `sm` and `xs`.

## Small side note

In your title, `marginTop: '-10'` is invalid, because it needs a unit. Use `'-10px'` or the number `-10`.

```jsx
<Title level={1} style={{ color: '#DDDCDC', marginTop: -10 }}>
```

**Which to choose?** Option 1 is lighter and avoids re-renders. Option 2 is handy if you want to keep everything in JS or change other props based on breakpoint.

